Migration chain for the ``platform`` schema — the single shared schema that
holds practices, users, identities, booking links and the platform audit log.

Run it with the ``platform`` section of ../alembic.ini:

    poetry run alembic -n platform upgrade head
    poetry run alembic -n platform revision --autogenerate -m "..."
    poetry run alembic -n platform current

Stamps land in ``platform.alembic_version_platform``. The tenant chain in
../alembic/ is a separate graph with separate bookkeeping — see env.py here for
why they are not one chain, and PABLO-k7it for why this one exists at all.

After any revision that changes DDL, regenerate the fresh-install template and
commit it alongside the revision:

    poetry run python backend/scripts/regen_platform_schema.py

CI enforces that the template matches this chain's head.
